# Signup form

`forms.lg` validation: an error summary, `.prevent`, a submit button disabled
while the form is invalid.

## Note

The form says `novalidate`: this page validates in `To submit:` and shows its
own messages, so the browser's built-in validation (which would stop `submit`
at the first field `type="email"` rejects) stays out of the way.

## Note

Two kinds of "is this valid": `errors` is a plain `State:` field, set only
inside `To submit:`, so nothing is scolded before the visitor has tried once.
`formValid` is a DERIVED `Bool`, recomputed from the live field values on
every keystroke, and only ever drives `disabled` on the submit button.

## To validate (email: Text) and (password: Text) and (confirmPassword: Text) -> Seq of FieldError:
    Let mutable e be noErrors().
    Set e to checkRequired(e, "email", email).
    Set e to checkEmail(e, "email", email).
    Set e to checkMinLength(e, "password", password, 8).
    Set e to checkSame(e, "confirmPassword", password, confirmPassword, "Passwords do not match.").
    Return e.

## To isFormValid (email: Text) and (password: Text) and (confirmPassword: Text) -> Bool:
    Return isValid(validate(email, password, confirmPassword)).

## Page /signup

State:
    Let email be "".
    Let password be "".
    Let confirmPassword be "".
    Let errors be a new Seq of FieldError.
    Let welcomed be false.
    Let formValid always be isFormValid(email, password, confirmPassword).

Actions:
    To submit:
        Set errors to validate(email, password, confirmPassword).
        If isValid(errors):
            Set welcomed to true.

View:
    <main class="signup card">
      <h1>Create an account</h1>
      <form id="signup" novalidate on-submit.prevent={submit}>
        {if length of errors is greater than 0:}
          <div id="summary" class="error-summary">
            <p>Please fix the following:</p>
            <ul>
              {for each e in errors, keyed by e's field:}
                <li class="summary-item">{e's message}</li>
              {end}
            </ul>
          </div>
        {end}
        <label for="email">Email</label>
        <input id="email" type="email" bind={email}>
        <p id="email-error" class="field-error">{errorFor(errors, "email")}</p>
        <label for="password">Password</label>
        <input id="password" type="password" bind={password}>
        <p id="password-error" class="field-error">{errorFor(errors, "password")}</p>
        <label for="confirm">Confirm password</label>
        <input id="confirm" type="password" bind={confirmPassword}>
        <p id="confirm-error" class="field-error">{errorFor(errors, "confirmPassword")}</p>
        <button id="submit-btn" type="submit" disabled={not formValid}>Sign up</button>
      </form>
      {if welcomed:}<p id="welcome">Welcome aboard.</p>{end}
    </main>

Style:
    .signup { max-width: 24rem; margin: 3rem auto; }
    .error-summary { border: 1px solid var(--accent); border-radius: var(--radius); padding: .5rem 1rem; margin-bottom: 1rem; }
    .field-error:empty { display: none; }

## Test: the button starts disabled and no errors show before a first attempt

Expect that "#submit-btn" is disabled.
Expect that "#summary" is hidden.

## Test: a bad submission names each problem and keeps the button disabled

Type "ada" into "#email".
Type "short" into "#password".
Type "short" into "#confirm".
Submit "#signup".
Expect that the text of "#email-error" is equal to "This does not look like an email address.".
Expect that the text of "#password-error" is equal to "Use at least 8 characters.".
Expect that the count of ".summary-item" is equal to 2.
Expect that "#submit-btn" is disabled.
Expect that "#welcome" is hidden.

## Test: mismatched passwords are refused even when both are long enough

Type "ada@example.com" into "#email".
Type "correct horse" into "#password".
Type "different horse" into "#confirm".
Expect that "#submit-btn" is disabled.
Submit "#signup".
Expect that the text of "#confirm-error" is equal to "Passwords do not match.".
Expect that "#welcome" is hidden.

## Test: the button stays disabled until every field is valid

Type "ada@example.com" into "#email".
Expect that "#submit-btn" is disabled.
Type "correct horse" into "#password".
Expect that "#submit-btn" is disabled.
Type "correct horse" into "#confirm".
Expect that "#submit-btn" is not disabled.

## Test: a good submission is accepted and clears the error summary

Type "ada@example.com" into "#email".
Type "correct horse" into "#password".
Type "correct horse" into "#confirm".
Expect that "#submit-btn" is not disabled.
Submit "#signup".
Expect that the text of "#welcome" is equal to "Welcome aboard.".
Expect that "#summary" is hidden.
